--- Partially applies the leading argument(s) of a function.
---
--- @details
--- `partial` takes `[f, bound]` where `bound` is a list of 1ÃÂÃÂ¢ÃÂÃÂÃÂÃÂ3
--- arguments to pre-fill, and returns an arrow awaiting the remaining
--- argument. `bound` lists longer than 3 elements are not supported --
--- `f` is returned unchanged in that case.
---
--- @example
--- `add3 :: [a, b, c] ~> a + b + c`
--- `add_from_10 :: [add3, [10, 20]] >>> comb.partial`
--- `5 >>> add_from_10`
--- -- => 35
---
export partial :: [f, bound] ~> match bound {
  [a]: x ~> f(a, x),
  [a, b]: x ~> f(a, b, x),
  [a, b, c]: x ~> f(a, b, c, x),
  _: f
}
